WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:07.275
Every AI agent you work with meets you as a stranger. Claude Code. Codex. Grok. Kimi. Hermes.

2
00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:14.838
Each new session starts from zero, and the work you did together lives inside someone else's product, or nowhere at all.

3
00:00:16.438 --> 00:00:18.996
RivetHub is the memory behind all of them.

4
00:00:19.055 --> 00:00:20.364
And it belongs to you.

5
00:00:22.164 --> 00:00:25.515
As you work, every session is captured automatically.

6
00:00:25.578 --> 00:00:29.309
Prompts, tool calls, and results, from every agent you use.

7
00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:32.596
No handoff docs, nothing to remember to write down.

8
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.999
It all lands on hardware you control.

9
00:00:36.499 --> 00:00:38.163
So your agents get to know you.

10
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:42.350
In the next session, in any tool, they search that record before they answer.

11
00:00:42.404 --> 00:00:46.108
The decision you made in Claude yesterday. Codex already knows today.

12
00:00:46.161 --> 00:00:51.583
Your preferences and corrections stick, and every answer links back to the conversation it came from.

13
00:00:53.083 --> 00:00:54.013
And it compounds.

14
00:00:54.068 --> 00:01:03.203
Sessions are folded into a tree of summaries, then distilled into a living wiki: what's true about your projects, your setup, and the lessons you learned the hard way.

15
00:01:03.258 --> 00:01:05.610
Every session starts smarter than the last.

16
00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.315
Because they share one memory, your agents work as a team.

17
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.747
One plans, another builds, another reviews.

18
00:01:12.802 --> 00:01:18.770
They hand work to each other and pick up exactly where the last one stopped, shaped around the way you work.

19
00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.601
And it stays yours. Fully open source, and self-hosted.

20
00:01:23.662 --> 00:01:29.840
It runs on the subscriptions and APIs you already use, so there's no new AI bill, and no middleman.

21
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.898
Switch providers, try a new agent, and your memory comes with you.

22
00:01:35.398 --> 00:01:42.027
The RivetHub apps bring it together, on desktop and Android, with chat, terminals, and your whole memory in one place.

23
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:45.202
Start with one machine, and add more when you need them.

24
00:01:46.702 --> 00:01:48.476
We built it for ourselves first.

25
00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:53.797
Since February, one memory has carried nearly a million messages across every model we've used.

26
00:01:53.853 --> 00:01:56.458
And it's still the first place our agents look.

27
00:01:58.258 --> 00:02:02.048
Your agents. Your memory. Your hardware. RivetHub.

28
00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.574
Get started at rivethub.io.
